From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] printers: make the char8_t conversion explicit

Clang 22 diagnoses the implicit char8_t to char32_t conversion as
-Wcharacter-conversion. GoogleTest enables -Werror for its own targets, so use
an explicit conversion for the intentional code-unit value conversion.
---
 googletest/include/gtest/gtest-printers.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/googletest/include/gtest/gtest-printers.h b/googletest/include/gtest/gtest-printers.h
index f783f253..a209ca41 100644
--- a/googletest/include/gtest/gtest-printers.h
+++ b/googletest/include/gtest/gtest-printers.h
@@ -525,7 +525,7 @@ inline void PrintTo(char16_t c, ::std::ostream* os) {
 }
 #ifdef __cpp_lib_char8_t
 inline void PrintTo(char8_t c, ::std::ostream* os) {
-  PrintTo(ImplicitCast_<char32_t>(c), os);
+  PrintTo(static_cast<char32_t>(c), os);
 }
 #endif
 
-- 
2.50.1
